      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1872, Governor Chauncey Cleveland’s efforts brought a railroad station to Hampton, reshaping the town’s connectivity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.hamptonct.org/visitor_info.htm",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hampton once housed a tannery and factories that produced pins, buttons, rakes, spectacles, hats, and silver spoons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.hamptonct.org/visitor_info.htm",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town was incorporated in 1786, carved out of Windham, Brooklyn, Pomfret, and Mansfield.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ct.one/towns/hampton",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hampton’s Congregational Church, still standing, is the second oldest church in Connecticut, with parts dating back to 1754.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hampton%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The two‑story House the Women Built, erected in 1776 by Sally Bowers and other women, stands as a testament to female ingenuity during the Revolutionary War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hampton%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "At Clark’s Corner, a liberty pole erected in 1849 still marks the town’s early patriotic spirit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
